      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When assessing the legitimacy of a protest, it’s critical to examine the broader context and the ultimate goals of the participants. Violence generally undermines civil protests as it can detract from the message and alienate public sympathy. Protesters are usually seeking change through nonviolent means, and violence may be perpetrated by a minority that does not represent the majority of participants. It is crucial to balance reporting both the peaceful nonviolent aspects of the demonstrations and any actions that diverge from peaceful protest. Believability comes from evaluating these factors holistically rather than focusing solely on the periods of unrest.",
